# Gitignored files copied into each new worktree (.gitignore syntax).
# Only files that match AND are gitignored are copied — tracked files never are.
#
# ALWAYS anchor a pattern with a leading `/`. Unanchored gitignore patterns match at
# any depth, and the copier tests them against `git ls-files --others --ignored`, which
# descends into an orphaned `.claude/worktrees/<name>` (a stray dir is not a repo
# boundary the way a registered worktree's `.git` file is). So bare `local.properties`
# also matched `.claude/worktrees/<name>/local.properties` and replicated the orphan's
# tree inside every new worktree, one level deeper each time. Negation does NOT fix
# this — `!.claude/worktrees/` has a trailing slash, so it matches directories only and
# never wins last-match against a file path. Anchoring does: a rooted pattern cannot
# match anything under `.claude/worktrees/`. See "Worktrees" in .agents/AGENTS.md.

# Android SDK location; :app Gradle builds fail without it.
/local.properties

# Local permission allowlist, so worktree sessions don't re-prompt for the same commands.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Server secrets/config if they ever land in a dotenv file (ESV_API_TOKEN, DATABASE_URL,
# JWT_SECRET, SMTP_*). Today these come from the shell / fly secrets, so these usually
# match nothing — harmless, and it means a new worktree keeps working if that changes.
/.env
/.env.local
